<%- include('partials/header', {title: 'Blue/Green Deployment with Elastic Beanstalk'}) %>

<section class="project-hero">
  <a href="/" class="project-back-btn"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  <h1>Blue/Green Deployment with AWS Elastic Beanstalk</h1>
  <p>Zero-downtime deployment strategy using Elastic Beanstalk environment cloning, URL swap, and instant traffic switching between application versions.</p>
  <div class="project-hero-tags">
    <span>Elastic Beanstalk</span><span>Blue/Green</span><span>Auto Scaling</span><span>Load Balancer</span><span>Zero Downtime</span>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="project-details">
  <div class="center">
    <img src="/images/blue-green.png" alt="Blue/Green Deployment Architecture" class="project-diagram">
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Project Overview</h3>
    <p>This project demonstrates <strong>Blue/Green deployment</strong> using AWS Elastic Beanstalk — enabling <strong>zero-downtime releases</strong> by maintaining two identical production environments and swapping URLs instantly.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Created Elastic Beanstalk app with load-balanced, auto-scaling environment.</li>
      <li>Deployed sample Tomcat app to the <strong>Blue environment</strong>.</li>
      <li><strong>Cloned the environment</strong> to create the Green environment.</li>
      <li>Deployed updated version to Green and executed <strong>URL swap</strong>.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Architecture Explanation</h3>
    <div class="architecture-grid">
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🔵 Blue (Production)</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Serving <strong>live traffic</strong> with stable version</li>
          <li>ELB + Auto Scaling Group</li>
          <li>Original application URL</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🟢 Green (Staging)</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Cloned environment with <strong>new version</strong></li>
          <li>Fully tested before swap</li>
          <li>Becomes production after URL swap</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🔄 URL Swap</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Instant traffic switch</strong> — no downtime</li>
          <li>Blue becomes rollback target</li>
          <li>DNS-level environment swap</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Implementation Steps</h3>
    <div class="steps-grid">
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">1</div><p>Created Beanstalk app with <strong>Load Balancing, Auto-scaling</strong> environment type.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">2</div><p>Deployed sample Tomcat app to <strong>Blue environment</strong>.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">3</div><p>Used <strong>Clone</strong> feature to create identical Green environment.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">4</div><p>Modified index.jsp ("New version") and deployed to <strong>Green environment</strong>.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">5</div><p>Performed <strong>URL swap</strong> — original URL now points to new version instantly.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Key Learnings</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Understood <strong>Blue/Green deployment</strong> for zero-downtime releases.</li>
      <li>Used Beanstalk's <strong>Clone feature</strong> to duplicate environments.</li>
      <li>Practiced <strong>application versioning</strong> and deployment management.</li>
      <li>Understood <strong>rollback strategies</strong> — Blue stays live until Green is confirmed.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="center">
    <a href="/" class="btn-back"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  </div>
</div>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
